//
// fileio.pla -- the maux FILEIO module (milestone 3, docs/PLASMA-
// PORT.md). Copied from Dave Schmenk's PLASMA
// (~/src/PLASMA/src/libsrc/apple/fileio.pla) and retargeted for maux.
// maux's SYS_* numbers ARE the ProDOS MLI numbers, and every call
// here rides cmdsys:syscall(cmd, params) (rt.pla's syscall, already
// retargeted to the raw $FF00 gate), so the whole a2*/a1*/a3* file --
// open/close/read/write/create/destroy/GFI/SFI/GET_EOF/SET_EOF/
// GET_MARK/SET_MARK/GET_PREFIX/SET_PREFIX -- maps UNCHANGED. Only
// THREE things are retargeted, per docs/PLASMA-PORT.md M3:
//
// 1. io_buffers are KERNEL-owned on maux, not process-owned. The
//    upstream a2open() reserves a 1024-byte heap buffer per open file
//    and passes its address in the MLI OPEN parmlist's io_buffer
//    field; on maux that field is REWRITTEN by the kernel (a process-
//    bank address there points at garbage in main RAM once the MLI
//    dereferences it outside the process's bank -- see src/bin/cat.s's
//    header, and the ratified convention it cites, docs/USERLAND.md
//    "ABI RESOLUTIONS"). So a2open() below always passes io_buffer =
//    $0000, and there is no per-file iobuf_addr/iobuf_ref bookkeeping
//    left to do -- a2close() and a23read()/a2write() etc. no longer
//    need to hunt for "which slot owns this refnum" at all, they just
//    pass the refnum straight through. a2iobufs() (fileio:iobufalloc,
//    called by plasm.pla as `fileio:iobufalloc(2)`) becomes a true
//    no-op that returns success without touching the heap -- maux
//    needs no per-file buffers to reserve, and the caller (plasm.pla)
//    discards its return value anyway.
//
// 2. maux has no MLI NEWLINE ($C9) -- the kernel's SYS_* table does
//    not wire that call number (docs/SYSCALL.md), so a2newline() must
//    NOT syscall it (it would come back ERR_P8_UNWIRE-shaped). Instead
//    it records (emask, nlchar) per refnum in a small module-local
//    table (nl_emask[]/nl_char[], indexed directly by refnum -- ProDOS
//    ref_nums are small integers and maux's own open-file pool tops
//    out at 8, docs/IOBUF-LENDING.md; NL_MAX=16 gives headroom). Then
//    a23read() -- fileio:read, the ONLY read path plasm's lexer uses
//    (toolsrc/lex.pla:352, `fileio:read(refnum, inptr, inlen)`) --
//    checks that table: if a mode is set for the refnum, it does the
//    plain MLI READ of up to `len` bytes, scans the bytes returned for
//    the first where `(byte & emask) == nlchar`, and if found, calls
//    the file back to just past that byte with SET_MARK ($CE) (via
//    the already-present a23getmark/a23setmark helpers) and returns
//    the length up to and including it; not found, or no mode set, is
//    a plain read of the full transfer. This is EXACTLY the emulation
//    proshimcr.s already does for the same reason on the same kernel
//    (src/bin/proshimcr.s PS_NEWLIN/PS_READ) -- same mark arithmetic
//    (mark_after_read - (trans_count - (index+1)) == mark_before_read
//    + index + 1), reimplemented here in PLASMA instead of hand-rolled
//    6502 because this module runs AS bytecode, not as an inline-asm
//    MLI adapter.
//
// 3. No language-card pokes to remove -- there were none in the
//    original file to begin with (no BIT ROMEN / LCRD / $C08x site;
//    checked in full). maux runs this in main RAM regardless.
//
// 4. TEXT IS READ IN EITHER MAUX CONVENTION (PLASM-FIX, docs/PLASM-
//    FIX-NOTES.md). plasm's lexer is Dave's UNMODIFIED source and
//    compares against low-ASCII literals (`== ' '`, `>= '0'`, a
//    line end of an unmasked `== $0D`); a file that `vi` or `cat >`
//    wrote on maux is high-bit ASCII ending $8D (README "Text"), and
//    every one of those comparisons failed: `INCLUDE "inc/..."` was
//    "Missing INCLUDE file". ProDOS's NEWLINE call has no word for
//    this because it never needed one -- but its MASK does: a mode
//    armed with a mask that ignores bit 7 ($7F, the one plasm arms)
//    is a request for TEXT, where bit 7 is not significant. So
//    a23read() clears bit 7 of every byte it returns under such a
//    mode, in the same pass that looks for the line end. A file in
//    either convention reads as low ASCII with a $0D line end, and
//    nothing that reads binary (no newline mode) is touched.
//
// 5. PLASM ONLY: `inc/NAME` FALLS BACK TO /usr/inc/NAME, READ ONLY.
//    Dave's PLASMA finds `include "inc/cmdsys.plh"` relative to the
//    PREFIX it runs from, where its distribution keeps inc/. A maux
//    user's cwd is a project directory; the headers live in /usr/inc.
//    The fallback is NOT in this file's code: it is ADDED, at the
//    //@INCFB markers below, by scripts/splice_fileio.py from
//    src/plasma/fileio.frag.pla, into the copy of FILEIO that plascut
//    links into /bin/plasm (Makefile $(PLASMFIO_DIR)) and nowhere else.
//    nas and every other tool link this file as it stands, with no
//    fallback code at all (xplasm does not fold a `const` switch, so
//    "off" used to cost 228 bytes of dead code in every cooked tool).
//    In the plasm build, when an open of a relative `inc/...` path fails
//    it is retried once as a READ-INTENT open ($83, OPEN-RO-2) of
//    /usr/inc/..., keeping the first failure's error if that fails too.
//    Read-only on purpose: a write must never land on a system header.
//    And once plasm has tried to DESTROY or CREATE a file the fallback is
//    off for the rest of the run, so `plasm src inc/cmdsys.plh` from a
//    directory with no inc/ reports the open of its OUTPUT failing
//    instead of "succeeding" into a read-only header.
//
// 6. NEWLINE MODE DIES WITH THE FILE. ProDOS resets a refnum's
//    newline mode on CLOSE; the table below did not, and refnums are
//    reused, so a later binary read on the same refnum was cut at the
//    first $0D (already so on the base) and, since change 4, bit-
//    stripped. a2open clears the entry on every successful open (that
//    covers every reuse of a refnum); a2close does not need to.
//
// The exported table (fileio.plh's t_fileio struc / the `word
// fileio[]` array below) is IDENTICAL in shape and order to upstream
// -- plasm.mod imports it by that contract -- only the a2iobufs/
// a2open/a2close/a2newline/a23read BODIES change.
//
include "inc/cmdsys.plh"
include "inc/fileio.plh"
//
// SOS access modes
//
//
//
const O_READ       = 1
const O_WRITE      = 2
const O_READ_WRITE = 3
//
// External interface
//
predef a2getpfx(path), a2setpfx(path), a2getfileinfo(path, fileinfo), a2setfileinfo(path, fileinfo), a23geteof(refnum)#2, a23seteof(refnum, eofl, eofh), a2iobufs(iobufs), a2open(path), a2close(refnum)
predef a23read(refnum, buf, len), a2write(refnum, buf, len), a2create(path, type, aux), a23destroy(path), a23rename(path, newpath)
predef a2newline(refnum, emask, nlchar), a2online(unit, buf), a2readblock(unit, buf, block), a2writeblock(unit, buf, block)
predef a23getmark(refnum)#2, a23setmark(refnum, eofl, eofh)
//
// Exported function table.
//
word fileio[]
word = @a2getpfx, @a2setpfx, @a2getfileinfo, @a2setfileinfo, @a23geteof, @a23seteof, @a2iobufs, @a2open, @a2close
word = @a23read, @a2write, @a2create, @a23destroy, @a23rename
word = @a2newline, @a2online, @a2readblock, @a2writeblock, @a23getmark, @a23setmark
//
// SOS/ProDOS error code
//
export byte perr
//
// maux NEWLINE emulation table (change 2 above). Index 0 is unused
// (refnum 0 is never a valid open file); nl_emask[r] == 0 means "no
// newline mode for refnum r", which is also upstream ProDOS's own
// sense of an all-zero enable mask, so no separate on/off flag is
// needed.
//
//@INCFB-DECL@
const NL_MAX = 16
byte nl_emask[NL_MAX + 1]
byte nl_char[NL_MAX + 1]
//
// ProDOS/SOS routines
//
def a1getpfx(path)
    ^path = 0
    return path
end
def a2getpfx(path)
    byte params[3]

    ^path    = 0
    params.0 = 1
    params:1 = path
    perr     = syscall($C7, @params)
    return path
end
def a3getpfx(path)
    byte params[4]

    params.0 = 2
    params:1 = path
    params.3 = 64
    perr     = syscall($C7, @params)
    return path
end
def a1setpfx(path)
    return path
end
def a2setpfx(path)
    byte params[3]

    params.0 = 1
    params:1 = path
    perr     = syscall($C6, @params)
    return path
end
def a3setpfx(path)
    byte params[6]
    byte fileinfo[2]
    char fullpath[65]

    if ^path and ^(path + 1) <> '/' and ^(path + 1) <> '.'
        a3getpfx(@fullpath)
        strcat(@fullpath, path)
        path = @fullpath
    fin
    params.0 = 3
    params:1 = path
    params:3 = @fileinfo
    params.5 = 2
    if not syscall($C4, @params) and (fileinfo.1 == $00 or fileinfo.1 == $0F) // Make sure it's a directory
        params.0 = 1
        params:1 = path
        syscall($C6, @params)
    else
        a3getpfx(path) // Get current path
    fin
    return path
end
def a1getfileinfo(path, fileinfo)
    perr = $01
    return perr
end
def a2getfileinfo(path, fileinfo)
    byte params[18]

    params.0 = 10
    params:1 = path
    perr     = syscall($C4, @params)
    memcpy(fileinfo, @params + 3, 15)
    return perr
end
def a3getfileinfo(path, fileinfo)
    byte params[6]

    params.0 = 3
    params:1 = path
    params:3 = fileinfo
    params.5 = 15
    perr     = syscall($C4, @params)
    return perr
end
def a1setfileinfo(path, fileinfo)
    perr = $01
    return perr
end
def a2setfileinfo(path, fileinfo)
    byte params[14]

    params.0 = 7
    params:1 = path
    memcpy(@params + 3, fileinfo, 11)
    perr     = syscall($C3, @params)
    return perr
end
def a3setfileinfo(path, fileinfo)
    byte params[6]

    params.0 = 3
    params:1 = path
    params:3 = fileinfo
    params.5 = 15
    perr     = syscall($C3, @params)
    return perr
end
def a1geteof(refnum)#2
    return 0, 0
end
def a23geteof(refnum)#2
    byte params[5]

    params.0 = 2
    params.1 = refnum
    params:2 = 0
    params.4 = 0
    syscall($D1, @params)
    return params:2, params.4
end
def a1seteof(refnum, eofl, eofh)
    return -1
end
def a23seteof(refnum, eofl, eofh)
    byte params[5]

    params.0 = 2
    params.1 = refnum
    params:2 = eofl
    params.4 = eofh
    perr = syscall($D0, @params)
    return perr
end
def a1getmark(refnum)#2
    return 0, 0
end
def a23getmark(refnum)#2
    byte params[5]

    params.0 = 2
    params.1 = refnum
    params:2 = 0
    params.4 = 0
    syscall($CF, @params)
    return params:2, params.4
end
def a1setmark(refnum, eofl, eofh)
    return -1
end
def a23setmark(refnum, eofl, eofh)
    byte params[5]

    params.0 = 2
    params.1 = refnum
    params:2 = eofl
    params.4 = eofh
    perr = syscall($CE, @params)
    return perr
end
def a1open(path)
    return 0
end
//
// (change 1) No per-file heap buffers on maux -- the kernel owns
// io_buffers. Upstream reserved MAX_IOBUFS-1 extra 1024-byte buffers
// via heapallocalign(); here there is nothing to allocate, and
// plasm.pla's `fileio:iobufalloc(2)` discards the return value, so a
// bare success return is the whole contract.
//
def a2iobufs(iobufs)
    return 0
end
def a13iobufs(iobufs)
    return 0
end
//
// (change 1) a2open no longer hunts for an iobuf slot -- there are
// none. io_buffer = $0000 (maux/kernel-owned; see file header).
//
def a2open(path)
    byte params[6]
    //@INCFB-LOCALS@

    params.0 = 3
    params:1 = path
    params:3 = 0
    params.5 = 0
    perr     = syscall($C8, @params)
    //@INCFB-BLOCK@
    if params.5 and params.5 <= NL_MAX
        nl_emask[params.5] = 0          // (change 6) a new file, no mode
    fin
    return params.5
end
def a3open(path)
    byte params[7]

    params.0 = 4
    params:1 = path
    params.3 = 0
    params:4 = 0
    params.6 = 0
    perr = syscall($C8, @params)
    return params.3
end
def a1close(refnum)
    return perr
end
//
// (change 1) a2close no longer checks an iobuf_ref table before
// closing -- upstream REFUSED to close (leaving the file open!) when
// the refnum did not match a tracked slot; on maux every open refnum
// is real (the kernel, not this module, owns the buffer), so close it
// unconditionally.
//
def a2close(refnum)
    byte params[2]

    params.0 = 1
    params.1 = refnum
    perr     = syscall($CC, @params)
    return perr
end
def a3close(refnum)
    byte params[2]

    params.0 = 1
    params.1 = refnum
    perr     = syscall($CC, @params)
    return perr
end
def a1read(refnum, buf, len)
    return perr
end
//
// (change 2) fileio:read -- the ONLY read path plasm's lexer calls.
// Plain MLI READ, then if a NEWLINE mode is armed for this refnum
// (nl_emask[refnum] <> 0), scan the bytes just transferred for the
// first where (byte & emask) == nlchar; if found, wind the file mark
// back to just past it (GET_MARK was already advanced by the READ, so
// the new mark is mark_after - (trans - (index+1))) and return
// index+1 instead of the full transfer count. (change 4) Under a
// mask that ignores bit 7, bit 7 is cleared on the way past.
//
def a23read(refnum, buf, len)
    byte params[8]
    byte emask, nlchar, b, text
    word i, marklo, delta
    byte markhi

    params.0 = 4
    params.1 = refnum
    params:2 = buf
    params:4 = len
    params:6 = 0
    perr     = syscall($CA, @params)
    len      = params:6
    if len and refnum <= NL_MAX
        emask = nl_emask[refnum]
        if emask
            nlchar = nl_char[refnum]
            //
            // (change 4) a mask that ignores bit 7 asks for TEXT:
            // return it low-ASCII whichever convention the file is in.
            //
            text = (emask & $80) == 0
            i = 0
            while i < len
                b = ^(buf + i)
                if text
                    b = b & $7F
                    ^(buf + i) = b
                fin
                b = b & emask
                if b == nlchar
                    marklo, markhi = a23getmark(refnum)
                    delta = len - (i + 1)
                    if isult(marklo, delta)
                        markhi--
                    fin
                    marklo = marklo - delta
                    a23setmark(refnum, marklo, markhi)
                    return i + 1
                fin
                i++
            loop
        fin
    fin
    return len
end
def a1write(refnum, buf, len)
    return perr
end
def a2write(refnum, buf, len)
    byte params[8]

    params.0 = 4
    params.1 = refnum
    params:2 = buf
    params:4 = len
    params:6 = 0
    perr     = syscall($CB, @params)
    return params:6
end
def a3write(refnum, buff, len)
    byte params[6]

    params.0 = 3
    params.1 = refnum
    params:2 = buff
    params:4 = len
    perr     = syscall($CB, @params)
    return perr ?? 0 :: len
end
def a1create(path, type, aux)
    return perr
end
def a2create(path, type, aux)
    byte params[12]

    params.0  = 7
    params:1  = path
    params.3  = $C3
    params.4  = type
    params:5  = aux
    params.7  = type == $0F ?? $0D :: $01
    params:8  = 0
    params:10 = 0
    //@INCFB-STOP@
    perr      = syscall($C0, @params)
    return perr
end
def a3create(path, type, aux)
    byte params[6]
    byte options[4]

    params.0  = 3
    params:1  = path
    params:3  = @options
    params.5  = 4
    options.0 = type
    options:1 = aux
    options.3 = type == $0F ?? $0D :: $01
    perr      = syscall($C0, @params)
    return perr
end
def a1destroy(path)
    perr = $01
    return perr
end
def a23destroy(path)
    byte params[3]

    params.0 = 1
    params:1 = path
    //@INCFB-STOP@
    perr     = syscall($C1, @params)
    return perr
end
def a1rename(oldpath, newpath)
    perr = $01
    return perr
end
def a23rename(path, newpath)
    byte params[5]

    params.0 = 2
    params:1 = path
    params:3 = newpath
    perr     = syscall($C2, @params)
    return perr
end
def a1newline(refnum, emask, nlchar)
    return perr
end
//
// (change 2) a2newline no longer syscalls $C9 -- maux's kernel does
// not wire MLI NEWLINE. It just arms the per-refnum table a23read()
// checks. emask == 0 (upstream's own "off" sentinel) leaves the entry
// clear.
//
def a2newline(refnum, emask, nlchar)
    if refnum <= NL_MAX
        nl_emask[refnum] = emask
        nl_char[refnum]  = nlchar
    fin
    perr = 0
    return perr
end
def a3newline(refnum, emask, nlchar)
    byte params[4]

    params.0 = 3
    params.1 = refnum
    params.2 = emask ?? $FF :: $00
    params.3 = nlchar
    perr     = syscall($C9, @params)
    return perr
end
def a1online(unit, buf)
    perr = $27 // IOERR
    return perr
end
def a2online(unit, buf)
    byte params[4]

    params.0 = 2
    params.1 = unit
    params:2 = buf
    perr     = syscall($C5, @params)
    return perr
end
def a3volume(unit, volname)
    byte devname[17]
    byte info[11]
    byte params[9]

    ^volname = 0
    params.0 = 4
    params.1 = unit
    params:2 = @devname
    params:4 = @info
    params.6 = 11
    if syscall($85, @params) == 0
        params.0 = 4
        params:1 = @devname
        params:3 = volname
        params:5 = 0
        params:7 = 0
        return syscall($C5, @params)
    fin
    return -1
end
def a3online(unit, buf)
    byte info[11]
    byte volname[17]
    byte i

    if unit == 0
        for i = $01 to $0F
            if a3volume(i, buf) == 0
                ^buf = ^buf | (i << 4)
            fin
            buf = buf + 16
        next
    else
        return a3volume(unit, buf)
    fin
    return 0
end
def a13readblock(unit, buf, block)
    perr = $27  // IOERR
    return perr
end
def a2readblock(unit, buf, block)
    byte params[6]

    params.0 = 3
    params.1 = unit
    params:2 = buf
    params:4 = block
    perr     = syscall($80, @params)
    return perr
end
def a13writeblock(unit, buf, block)
    perr = $27  // IOERR
    return perr
end
def a2writeblock(unit, buf, block)
    byte params[6]

    params.0 = 3
    params.1 = unit
    params:2 = buf
    params:4 = block
    perr     = syscall($81, @params)
    return perr
end
//
// Machine specific initialization. maux's MACHID ($B0, IIe|128K --
// rt.pla) matches neither MACHID_III nor MACHID_I, so it falls
// through `otherwise` unchanged, same as real Apple II ProDOS: the
// default a2*/a23* table above stands.
//
when MACHID & MACHID_MODEL
    is MACHID_III
        fileio:getpfx      = @a3getpfx
        fileio:setpfx      = @a3setpfx
        fileio:getfileinfo = @a3getfileinfo
        fileio:setfileinfo = @a3setfileinfo
        fileio:iobufalloc  = @a13iobufs
        fileio:open        = @a3open
        fileio:close       = @a3close
        fileio:write       = @a3write
        fileio:create      = @a3create
        fileio:newline     = @a3newline
        fileio:online      = @a3online
        fileio:readblock   = @a13readblock
        fileio:writeblock  = @a13writeblock
        break
    is MACHID_I
        fileio:getpfx      = @a1getpfx
        fileio:setpfx      = @a1setpfx
        fileio:getfileinfo = @a1getfileinfo
        fileio:setfileinfo = @a1setfileinfo
        fileio:geteof      = @a1geteof
        fileio:seteof      = @a1seteof
        fileio:getmark     = @a1getmark
        fileio:setmark     = @a1setmark
        fileio:iobufalloc  = @a13iobufs
        fileio:open        = @a1open
        fileio:close       = @a1close
        fileio:read        = @a1read
        fileio:write       = @a1write
        fileio:create      = @a1create
        fileio:destroy     = @a1destroy
        fileio:rename      = @a1rename
        fileio:newline     = @a1newline
        fileio:online      = @a1online
        fileio:readblock   = @a13readblock
        fileio:writeblock  = @a13writeblock
        break
    otherwise // Apple ][ (and maux)
wend
//
// Keep module in memory
//
return modkeep
done
